   "category": "departure",
   "brief": "Single, sound; in the 'good eye' idiom, generous (Matthew 6:22; Luke 11:34).",
   "context": "In Matthew the saying sits between treasure in heaven and serving Mammon, and the 'evil eye' that follows is a known Jewish idiom for stinginess, so 'generous' fits the context.\n\n**The standard view.** Most translations use 'healthy' or 'sound', keeping the physical image of the eye, and mention generosity in a footnote. The physical image is lost with 'generous'.\n\nScholars disagree on this word, and this rendering is an editorial choice.",
